BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:
Section 1.
That Sections 8.60.181, Notice to Lietholder and 8.60.182, Junk Vehicle
Impoundment—Transfer of Title to the City, of Chapter 8.60, Nuisances, of Title 8, Health and
Safety, of the Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, are hereby created as set out in this
ordinance.
Sections currently existing within Chapter 8.60 not set out within this ordinance
remain unchanged.
8.60.181
Notice to lienholder.
Upon abatement by impoundment of any junk vehicle, as defined in Section 8.60.080, the
city shall provide written notification to any lienholder of record, stating the grounds for removal
and the name of the garage or place of impoundment of such vehicle.
Notice shall not be
required if the retail value of the junk vehicle is less than two thousand dollars ($2,000.00), as
determined by the nuisance officer, as defined in Section 8.60.020. The city shall forward a copy
of the notice to the owner and the person in charge of the garage or place of impoundment.
8.60.182
Junk Vehicle Impoundment—Transfer of Title to the City.
If the city has abated any junk vehicle by impoundment, and the owner or lietholder of
the junk vehicle fails to reclaim such junk vehicle and pay the costs of the abatement within
thirty (30) calendar days after the abatement by impoundment, title to the junk vehicle shall vest
in the city. If the owner of the junk vehicle fails to reclaim any personal property located inside
the junk vehicle during the impoundment period, the city shall dispose of that personal property
at the conclusion of the impoundment period. A change in title to the impounded junk vehicle
may be obtained by the city according to the authority of this chapter and the procedure
established in state statutes to obtain a change in title. Ifthejunk vehicle is sold by the city and
a balance remains after all the citj, ‘s costs of abatement are reimbursed, said balance shall be
returned to originaljunk vehicle owner.
Section 2.
That this ordinance shall be in flail force and effect upon its approval and
publication.
FIRST READING:
